      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When a state is facing imminent civil collapse, the immediate priority must be the preservation of life and the prevention of mass violence, which grants the government temporary, limited powers. However, these emergency measures must be strictly time-bound, narrowly tailored to the immediate threat, and subject to swift, transparent judicial review. If the \"brake\" becomes a permanent mechanism to silence opposition, then the state has abandoned its duty to protect its people and has become the primary source of instability.",
      "source": "target",
